 "text": "Hello there! How are you today? Of course! How old is your toddler? That's a good age for group picnic. Do you have a good spot in your neighborhood with lots of green space without too many steps? Some toddlers chew grapes or spill juice, so it' a good rule follow. Sandwiches, fruit, crackers, and cheese are easy snacks. A giant picture book is a lovely way to keep them engaged. You can read a page together, then let the toddler flip the next page themselves. Lots of open space and a shade tree if the sun comes out. A big blanket is handy for sitting on too. Yes, for those little hands get dirty.",
